<BaseLayout title="Install Honeybee-PH | PH-Tools" activePage="honeybee-ph">
  <div class="content-page">
    <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/honeybee-ph/">Honeybee-PH</a> / Install</p>
    <h1>Install Honeybee-PH</h1>
    <p>Honeybee-PH and its Grasshopper components are free and open-source.</p>

    <h2>YouTube walk-through</h2>
    <p>This video walks through installing both Ladybug Tools and Honeybee-PH:</p>
    <p><a href="https://youtu.be/DvH_Wxf1D8A" target="_blank">Installation walk-through</a></p>

    <h2>Requirements</h2>
    <p>Before installing, make sure you have:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://www.rhino3d.com/" target="_blank">Rhino-3D v8</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.ladybug.tools/" target="_blank">Ladybug-Tools v1.8</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://wufi.de/en/software/wufi-passive/" target="_blank">WUFI-Passive</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://passivehouse.com/04_phpp/04_phpp.htm" target="_blank">PHPP v9 or v10</a></li>
      <li>Windows 10+ or macOS 13+</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="callout warning">
      <strong>Note:</strong> Honeybee-PH does <strong>not</strong> include
      <a href="https://wufi.de/en/software/wufi-passive/" target="_blank">WUFI-Passive</a> or
      <a href="https://passivehouse.com/04_phpp/04_phpp.htm" target="_blank">PHPP</a>.
      You need to purchase those programs separately. Honeybee-PH builds and exports models for them.
    </div>

    <h2>Rhino / Grasshopper installation</h2>
    <p>To install Honeybee-PH:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Install Rhino v8 if you don't have it already.</li>
      <li><strong>Windows:</strong> Install Ladybug Tools with the <a href="https://app.pollination.cloud/cad-plugins" target="_blank">One-Click Installer for Grasshopper</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>macOS:</strong> Install Ladybug Tools with the <a href="https://www.food4rhino.com/en/app/ladybug-tools" target="_blank">Food4Rhino Installer</a>.</li>
      <li>
        In Grasshopper, run the "LB Versioner" component to update Ladybug Tools to the latest release.
        <img src="/img/install/lb_versioner.png" alt="LB Versioner component in Grasshopper" />
      </li>
      <li>
        Download the installer:
        <a href="https://github.com/PH-Tools/honeybee_grasshopper_ph/releases/latest/download/hbph_installer.ghx" class="btn btn-primary" style="margin-left: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.85rem;">Download Installer</a>
      </li>
      <li>Open <code>hbph_installer.ghx</code> in Rhino/Grasshopper and follow the on-screen prompts. On Windows, if you hit a permissions error, open Rhino as administrator.</li>
      <li>Restart Rhino and Grasshopper so the new components load.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Install trouble?</h2>
    <p>If you hit errors during setup, check these common causes:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Rhino version:</strong> You need Rhino v8. Honeybee-PH does not run on earlier versions.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Windows installer:</strong> Use the Ladybug Tools
        <a href="https://app.pollination.cloud/cad-plugins" target="_blank">One-Click Installer for Grasshopper</a> on Windows.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Ladybug Tools health:</strong> Drop the Honeybee "HB Check Versions" component onto the canvas to verify your Python, Radiance, and OS installs.
        <img src="/img/install/hb_config.png" alt="HB Check Versions component" />
      </li>
      <li><strong>Ladybug Tools version:</strong> You need v1.8 or later. Run "LB Versioner" to update.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Pollination installs:</strong> <a href="https://www.pollination.cloud/" target="_blank">Pollination</a> can place Ladybug Tools in a protected folder. If the installer fails with a permissions error, run Rhino as administrator.
        <img src="/img/install/run_admin.png" alt="Run Rhino as Administrator" />
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Error on Windows?</h2>
    <p>Windows installs occasionally fail because of a stray Python folder. To fix it:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Open File Explorer and go to <code>C:\Users\&lt;your-username&gt;\AppData\Roaming\</code>.</li>
      <li>
        Look for a folder named <code>Python</code>.
        <img src="/img/install/bad_python.png" alt="Unexpected Python directory" />
      </li>
      <li>If that <code>Python</code> folder exists, <strong>delete it</strong>. It shouldn't be there.</li>
      <li>Run the Grasshopper installer again.</li>
    </ol>

    <div class="callout">
      <strong>Still stuck?</strong> See the <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> page to reach us.
    </div>

    <h2>Manual installation</h2>
    <p>
      If you can't run the automatic installer, for example when IT policy blocks running Rhino as administrator,
      you can install manually. Most users should stick with the automatic installer.
    </p>

    <h3>Step 1: Locate your ladybug_tools folder</h3>
    <p>For most users, this is:</p>
    <div class="path-block">C:\Program Files\ladybug_tools\</div>
    <p>On some systems, it is here instead:</p>
    <div class="path-block">C:\Users\&lt;Your-User-Name&gt;\ladybug_tools\</div>

    <h3>Step 2: Open PowerShell</h3>
    <p>Open PowerShell from the Windows Start menu.</p>

    <h3>Step 3: Install the Python libraries</h3>
    <p>Run the command that matches your <code>ladybug_tools</code> path:</p>
    <div class="path-block">C:\"Program Files"\ladybug_tools\python\python -m pip install honeybee-ph PHX</div>
    <p><em>OR</em></p>
    <div class="path-block">C:\Users\&lt;Your-User-Name&gt;\ladybug_tools\python\python -m pip install honeybee-ph PHX</div>

    <h3>Step 4: Check the install</h3>
    <p>Open <code>ladybug_tools\python\Lib\site-packages\</code> and confirm that <code>honeybee_ph</code>, <code>PHX</code>, and <code>ph_units</code> folders are present.</p>

    <h3>Step 5: Download the Grasshopper tools</h3>
    <p>Download the latest Honeybee-PH Grasshopper components:</p>
    <blockquote><a href="https://github.com/PH-Tools/honeybee_grasshopper_ph/archive/refs/heads/main.zip">Grasshopper Tools (zip)</a></blockquote>

    <h3>Step 6: Copy honeybee_ph_rhino</h3>
    <p>Unzip the download and copy the <code>honeybee_ph_rhino</code> folder into <code>ladybug_tools\python\lib\site-packages\</code>.</p>
    <img src="/img/install/copy_GH_libraries.png" alt="Copy Grasshopper libraries" />

    <h3>Step 7: Copy the user objects</h3>
    <p>Copy the <code>honeybee_grasshopper_ph\user_objects</code> folder into your Grasshopper UserObjects folder:</p>
    <div class="path-block">C:\Users\&lt;Your-User-Name&gt;\AppData\Roaming\Grasshopper\UserObjects\</div>
    <img src="/img/install/copy_GH_components.png" alt="Copy Grasshopper components" />

    <h3>Step 8: Download Component-IO</h3>
    <p>Download the Grasshopper Component-IO library:</p>
    <blockquote><a href="https://github.com/PH-Tools/PH_GH_Component_IO/archive/refs/heads/main.zip">Grasshopper Component-IO (zip)</a></blockquote>

    <h3>Step 9: Copy ph_gh_component_io</h3>
    <p>Copy the <code>ph_gh_component_io</code> folder into <code>ladybug_tools\python\lib\site-packages\</code>.</p>
    <img src="/img/install/copy_GH_IO_library.png" alt="Copy Component-IO library" />

    <p>That's it. Open Rhino and Grasshopper and the Honeybee-PH components should be ready to use.</p>

    <div class="callout">
      <strong>Still stuck?</strong> See the <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> page to reach us.
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
